	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "edfS8mft14X3qv7Sa",
			"description": "Skitarii War-plate",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 5: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 5 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nVoid-sealed; can be worn in vacuum or a toxic/irradiated atmosphere without a separate rebreather, matching the environments Skitarii cohorts are routinely deployed into. Rigid heavy armour DX/Stealth penalties apply.\n\nLore: The moulded red plate worn by Skitarii Vanguard and Rangers, current Codex Adeptus Mechanicus background places it firmly in the same rigid-plate tier as an Astra Militarum carapace suit rather than anywhere near true power armour - Skitarii are tough, augmented humans in good armour, not the post-human, power-armoured Astartes their tactics are sometimes compared to.\n\nDesign: Torso DR set at the fixed Carapace anchor (framework.md, current value 70) per the assignment's own instruction that Skitarii war-plate is carapace-class, not a distinct Mechanicus armour tier. Non-torso DR matches the Imperium Carapace Armour, Tempestus Pattern's own proportions exactly (arm/leg/neck 64, skull 70, face 42, eye 20, hand 36, foot 42) rather than the plainer Guard Pattern's, since Skitarii war-plate is depicted as sealed, complete-coverage combat gear built for hazardous-environment operation - the same design brief the Tempestus Pattern's own full coverage (versus the Guard Pattern's bare hands) was built to answer - so this project reuses that reference point rather than re-deriving a third set of non-torso ratios with no lore reason to differ. TL11 (advanced Imperial/rare manufacture, matching plasma- and hellgun-tier Mechanicus production) and LC1 (Skitarii combat-issue, restricted outside the Cult Mechanicus, per framework.md's legality table) rather than the Guard's LC2 carapace bracket.",
