		{
			"id": "eQmJzeAfnbgrIv8mx",
			"description": "Sicarian Infiltration Armour",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 5: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 5 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nLighter and more flexible than standard war-plate; the reduced rigid-armour Stealth penalty is already reflected in the Stealth bonus above rather than stacked on top of it. Rigid heavy armour DX penalties still apply.\n\nLore: Sicarian Infiltrators and Ruststalkers wear a lighter, close-fitting variant of Skitarii war-plate built for infiltration, ambush and rapid close-quarters work rather than a Vanguard or Ranger cohort's firing line, current Codex Adeptus Mechanicus background consistently depicting Sicarian units as faster and quieter than line Skitarii at the cost of some raw protection.\n\nDesign: Kept at the same carapace-tier torso DR (70) as standard war-plate - the assignment's own \"carapace-class\" instruction applies to all Skitarii-adjacent armour in this file, and nothing in the lore suggests Sicarian units trade away their core plate's stopping power, only its bulk and completeness - but non-torso DR is scaled back down to the plainer Guard Pattern's own proportions (arm/leg/neck 52, skull 64, face 36, eye 20, hand 0, foot 36) and hands are left bare, reflecting a stripped-down suit built for speed and manual dexterity in close combat rather than full environmental sealing. The Stealth bonus (+2, matching the Imperium Mark X Phobos Pattern's own reduced-bulk logic) is this project's chosen mechanical hook for \"lighter and quieter than standard war-plate,\" reused from that entry's own precedent rather than invented fresh. Lower weight (22 lb vs. the War-plate's 32) follows directly from the reduced coverage and lighter plate. LC0 rather than the War-plate's LC1: Sicarian-pattern kit is chapter-restricted Cult Mechanicus material, per the Transonic Razor and Phosphor Serpenta's own LC0 reasoning in the weapons files.",
