		{
			"id": "eVBFmLXt-U4jyI-2m",
			"description": "Tech-Priest Robes, Armoured",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 7: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 7 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nFlexible armour: treat blunt/crushing damage that fails to penetrate as normal per the flexible-armour rule (blunt trauma still applies even when DR stops the attack). Worn under or woven into a Tech-Priest's ceremonial red robes, with no visible plate.\n\nLore: Senior Tech-Priests and Magi who do not wear full Skitarii war-plate are nonetheless rarely unarmoured: current Codex Adeptus Mechanicus background and Black Library depictions of Mechanicus characters (Belisarius Cawl among the more prominent) consistently show a fine metal-weave or ceramite-thread lining worked into the ubiquitous red robes, concealed enough that a stranger has no reason to suspect it.\n\nDesign: Built as the Mechanicus's own version of the Imperium Mesh Armour rather than a re-derived figure: torso DR taken directly from the fixed Mesh anchor (framework.md, current value 36, flexible), the same anchor the Imperium file's own hive-noble and assassin mesh armour uses, since a concealed metal-weave lining under robes is mechanically the same item as that entry regardless of who wears it or what colour the outer garment is - per framework.md's own instruction that the same underlying item gets the same numbers across factions. Non-torso DR and coverage follow the Mesh Armour entry's own \"a few below torso, nothing on hands/feet/head\" pattern exactly. TL11 and LC1 (Mechanicus-forged, not universally available) distinguish it from the Imperium entry's TL10/LC2 civilian-and-agent bracket, reflecting that this specific weave is a Cult Mechanicus product even though the underlying mesh technology is identical.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
