		{
			"id": "e3aJmX6j8_JYPI6D9",
			"description": "Mechadendrite Harness",
			"local_notes": "The physical backpack/spinal mount, power feed and control interface that lets a Tech-Priest carry and operate one or more mechadendrites; this entry is the mounting hardware only. The mechadendrite limb itself (an Extra Arm with appropriate reach/DX limitations, per framework.md's Adeptus Mechanicus section) is a trait defined in a traits file, not equipment, and is not included here - this harness exists so that trait has a priced, weighted physical object to attach to a character sheet's equipment list, the same separation of concerns the Storm Shield's force-field component and the Mechadendrite, Combat Tip weapon fitting already use elsewhere in this project.\n\nLore: Every mechadendrite-bearing Tech-Priest is depicted with some form of visible mounting rig - a spinal port, a backpack frame, an armoured harness - from which their extra limbs extend, consistent across current Codex Adeptus Mechanicus artwork and Black Library depictions of Tech-Priests from Enginseers to Archmagi.\n\nDesign: Deliberately holds no trait-granting content of its own: per this project's data-format rules, a mechadendrite's actual capability (reach, extra manipulation, a combat tip's weapon profile) belongs either to the Extra Arms trait (built by the traits agent) or to a weapon-fitting equipment entry like Mechadendrite, Combat Tip in the melee weapons file, never duplicated here. This entry is priced and weighted as a substantial piece of worn hardware (a spinal mount and power feed genuinely is bulky and expensive) precisely so that a character sheet shows the physical cost of carrying mechadendrites even though their mechanical benefit is recorded elsewhere. TL11 and LC1 (Mechanicus-forged bionic mounting hardware, restricted per framework.md's advanced-Imperial/rare bracket).",
			"tags": [
				"Gear",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "1500",
			"base_weight": "8 lb",
			"quantity": 1
		}
	]
